A||N||7||NOS3800||NOS 3800 vs SC3800 results||||8||
Z||000000||NOS3800||07-31-2001||12:14 AM||||Well, the results are in, the SC 3800's whoopped the NOS 3800. The two SC3800's one manual( JASON H.), the other auto( Earl S.) were running consistently 13.3's at 100mph! My car was running a PITIFUL 14.0-14.4. BUT, There was a problem, that I couldn't fix till I got home. My car was running WAY rich under NOS. After placing the NOS nozzle in a location that will let the car make FULL advantage of the NOS, it runs better now then it did when I ran a 13.58! So, can't wait to get back to the track.<P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||8
Z||000001||saleenfiero||07-31-2001||02:38 PM||||So the auto ran the same time as the manual SC3800?  What do you have NOS, stick or slushbox?<P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||1
Z||000002||pontiacs4me||07-31-2001||03:20 PM||||A good friend of mine has a SC3800 in a 91 lumina.  He also has nitrous.  His car ran 13.70 at 104 with no nitrous, and 12.87 at 111 with it.  His car weighs 3550 with him in it.  Why are our beloved fieros so slow.  With 800 less pounds we should be in the high 11's with similiar setups.  I have yet to hear of a v-6 fiero that is in the 12's.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||07-31-2001||03:50 PM||||pontiacs4me, wait a couple weeks, I bet either Earl S. or Jason H. will be in the 12s.  Neither of them have NOS either.  Bill might even get there soon with his 3800 N/A with NOS.<P>Also keep in mind a loaded 3800 GT will weigh in around 3000 lbs. with the auto tranny.  <p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 07-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||07-31-2001||03:53 PM||||What sort of tranny is the manula car running, what mods to they have on them? underdrive pulley's???<P>I'm planning a 3.8SC , already have the NOS to go on it , and was wondering what others have done<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Sleeper||07-31-2001||07:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pontiacs4me:<BR><B>I have yet to hear of a v-6 fiero that is in the 12's.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Chris West's 3.4 <B>TURBO</B> ran 11.99 in Palmdale(and that high elevation too), at least thats what i heard.<BR><P>------------------<BR>85 GT Auto<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels wrapped with Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering springs, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, West Coast Fiero Strut Tower Bar, West Coast Fiero Cold-Air Intake w/ HKS Super Flow filter, Beretta brake upgrade in front, KVS Performance Slotted Rotors in rear, Earl's Steel-Braided Brake Lines J.E.T. super chip and MSD Blaster Coil.||||reg||1
Z||000006||NOS3800||07-31-2001||08:21 PM||||Wait a minute, a Fiero with a SC3800 with smaller pulley running 11's???? Are you crazy. As a general rule, every 100 pounds you lose, you gain a tenth of a second. That Lumina you speak of, I also know about. He has more done to it then just being stock. <BR>Jason(who can correct me if I am wrong) runs a rather large 3.5 pulley and thats it. It is mated to a Getrag 5 speed tranny. He runs the 13.3's with tire spin. It is a coupe. <BR>Earl Sessions has a SC3800 with a 3.4 pulley, performance Computer, and Adjustable Fuel Pressure Reg. It is mated to the 4T65E auto tranny. At the GROVE he did not suffer tire spin and ran CONSISTANT 13.3's. However, at his home track in Southern MD, he has run 13.3's with tire spin through the 60 foot mark. Believe me, all they need to do is get a 3.25 pulley and slicks and you will have your 12 sec Fieros. BTW, these are consistant runs, which means they do it regularly, that Lumina may have only posted those fastest times once on a PERFECT nite. Jason and Earl and Bill for that matter have yet to race on that PERFECT nite!<BR>Bill's (NOS3800) has been running 13.5's while running EXTREMELY rich. The NOS was spraying through the MAF sensor which in turn caused the motor to had way too much fuel/NOS. I have resolved that, and now just need some new plugs. I have ran my times with a 75 shot, I can easily bump up to a 100-125 and also be a 12 sec Fiero. Mine has a NA 3800 mated to a 4T60E auto tranny. NOTHING else but NOS.<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000007||artherd||07-31-2001||11:37 PM||||If you think a 13.3sec quarter-mile car that handles like a 308 ferrari is slow, then there is just no helping you ;)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
